0248033106327057,"token":"."}],"message":{"content":"Echo State Networks (ESNs) are a type of recurrent neural network used for processing time-series data. They consist of a large, sparsely connected hidden layer, often referred to as the \"reservoir,\" which processes input data and passes it through without learning weights. The output is then learned from the reservoir's state using a simple linear regression. Reservoirs in ESNs are typically trained using random weights, focusing on capturing the dynamics of the input data rather than learning specific tasks.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":49219000,"total_duration":1390070600}}